From: Ethan Blanch <ethan.blanch@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 00:05:00 +1200
Subject: [PATCH] compat: include <signal.h> before the SYS_SECCOMP fallback

glibc declares SYS_SECCOMP as an enum constant in <bits/siginfo-consts.h>
(under _GNU_SOURCE, and only in newer releases). Defining the fallback macro
before <signal.h> is seen turns that enum into "1 = 1" and fails with
"expected identifier"; guarding on __ANDROID__ instead leaves it undeclared
on older glibc. Including <signal.h> first (hosted builds only; the loader
is freestanding) lets the fallback depend on what libc actually provides.
No change for bionic.
---
diff --git a/src/compat.h b/src/compat.h
index 53300b8..7b8abd1 100644
--- a/src/compat.h
+++ b/src/compat.h
@@ -261,6 +261,15 @@
 #    ifndef NT_ARM_SYSTEM_CALL
 #        define NT_ARM_SYSTEM_CALL		0x404
 #    endif
+#    /* Modified 2026-09-26 for uls-proot (github.com/ItsPhysip/uls-proot):
+     * include <signal.h> before the fallback.  glibc declares SYS_SECCOMP
+     * as an enum constant there (under _GNU_SOURCE); defining the macro
+     * first turns that enum into "1 = 1" and breaks static glibc builds.
+     * Skipped for the freestanding loader, which has no libc headers and
+     * never includes <signal.h>.  Bionic builds are unchanged. */
+#    if __STDC_HOSTED__
+#        include <signal.h>
+#    endif
 #    ifndef SYS_SECCOMP
 #        define SYS_SECCOMP 1
 #    endif
